================================================================================================
  [PASS] d_m T_A^{mn} + q F^{n a} J_a == 0 for all n (generic F_M, generic A_m(t,x,y,z))  [mediator exchanges momentum with the charge]  (residuals: [0, 0, 0, 0])
  [PASS] MUTATION CONTROL: dropping the eta^{mn} L term breaks the identity (test discriminates)
  [PASS] charged clock dust: d_m T_d^{mn} = + q F^{n a} J_a on its own equations (1+1, both components)  => total dark stress conserved
  [PASS] nonrelativistic dust acceleration = + q E = + q dV/dx  (E = d_x A_0 = d_x V)
  [PASS] AQUAL flux function is odd, positive for V'>0, negative for V'<0, and strictly increasing (f' = 1+(y-1)e^{-y} > 0)
  [PASS] => point charge: V' > 0 outward, acceleration +q V' points AWAY from the charge: like charges REPEL (healthy vector); the MOND-strength force on the dark dust has the ANTI-gravity sign
  => the ratio lock n = lambda rho_b is not even dynamically preserved: the charged dust is pushed OUT of the baryons by
     its own MOND-strength self-repulsion (sign SOLID; the resulting profile NOT-COMPUTED, but it cannot be the
     baryon-tracking one).  An ATTRACTIVE MOND self-force needs a scalar mediator = a second scalar (Case 4).
  Baryons: S_m[g,psi] is a separate diff-invariant functional with no A or T dependence  =>  grad_m T_b^{mn} = 0 is
